# Explicit native-screen mount API

Status: in progress; Phase 0 complete

Related design: `docs/non-owning-native-screen-mount-proposal.md`

## Purpose

Replace the ambiguous no-argument `ds.mount()` overload with an explicit
`ds.mountNativeScreen()` command. Component mounting remains
`ds.mount(component, options)`, while both entry points continue to use the
same one-current-mount lifecycle and `ds.unmount()` cleanup command.

DwarfSpec `0.2.0` has not been published. This is a clean API correction:
there is no compatibility alias, deprecation period, migration shim, or legacy
documentation requirement.

This checklist is the implementation completion contract. A phase is complete
only when every task and exit-gate item in that phase is checked and its fresh
evidence is recorded in the evidence ledger.

## Locked public contract

☐ Add `ds.mountNativeScreen()` with that exact spelling.
☐ Make `ds.mount(component, options)` exclusively responsible for component
  and complete-screen mounts.
☐ Reject both `ds.mount()` and `ds.mount(nil)` with an actionable diagnostic
  that directs the caller to `ds.mountNativeScreen()`.
☐ Reject arguments passed to `ds.mountNativeScreen()` instead of silently
  ignoring them.
☐ Do not retain the no-argument `ds.mount()` behavior as an alias.
☐ Keep `ds.unmount()` as the shared release operation for every mount kind.
☐ Keep the one-current-mount rule across both entry points.
☐ Return the borrowed native root subject from `ds.mountNativeScreen()`.
☐ Preserve `ds.root()`, `ds.get()`, `ds.inspect()`, input, pointer, redraw,
  capture, staleness, and cleanup behavior for native-screen mounts.
☐ Keep `ESubjectSource.NATIVE` and `ESubjectSource.OVERLAY` unchanged; they
  select subject hierarchies within a native-screen mount, not mount kinds.
☐ Do not introduce a mount-target string, target option, or mount-kind enum.
☐ Keep the current `0.2.0-1` version; this unpublished API correction does not
  require another version bump.

## Ownership and behavior invariants

☐ `ds.mountNativeScreen()` pins the exact current native DF viewscreen and its
  native widget root.
☐ It creates, shows, resizes, replaces, dismisses, and owns no `ZScreen` or
  native game screen.
☐ DFHack focus, viewscreen stack, current viewscreen, overlay registration,
  and native navigation remain externally owned.
☐ Native and registered-overlay input continues through the pinned native
  viewscreen and normal DFHack overlay dispatch.
☐ Native redraw continues to wait on the existing observed completed-render
  boundary unless `{wait=false}` is supplied.
☐ A changed current viewscreen continues to make the mount and its subjects
  stale instead of retargeting or navigating.
☐ Cleanup continues to restore pointer/button state, rendering
  instrumentation, and retained references without dismissing the screen.
☐ No runner transport, scheduler, persistence, CLI, or in-game runner UI
  behavior changes as part of this work.

