The inventory must remain search-driven. Add any other positive no-argument
mount call, public declaration, diagnostic, or example found during
implementation to this list and update it in the same change.

## Global engineering rules

☐ Add LuaDoc comments to every new or changed Lua function, method, and
  class-like module or table.
☐ Preserve the existing native attachment, interaction target, render
  observer, subject adapters, and cleanup stack instead of duplicating them.
☐ Keep public camel-case spelling and internal snake-case spelling consistent.
☐ Preserve unrelated worktree changes.
☐ Use Mermaid for any graph added or revised in documentation.
☐ Record only fresh verification evidence in this checklist.
☐ Do not add package-manifest or VS Code task-configuration tests.

