## Phase 1: Explicit public and internal entry points

Goal: separate component mounting from native-screen mounting without changing
the underlying mount lifecycle.

☐ Add `ds.mountNativeScreen(...)` to the run-scoped `ds` object.
☐ Validate that the command receives no arguments.
☐ Route the command through the existing native attachment factory and mount
  context.
☐ Refactor `ds.mount` to require a non-nil component and preserve its existing
  component options behavior.
☐ Give `ds.mount()` and `ds.mount(nil)` the same actionable
  `mountNativeScreen()` guidance.
☐ Rename `mount_context:mount_native(...)` to
  `mount_context:mount_native_screen(...)`.
☐ Update internal diagnostics to use “native-screen mount” when the mount kind
  matters and “native attachment” when describing the borrowed implementation
  resource.
☐ Keep the same mount ID, subject source, interaction target, cleanup entries,
  observer, and returned root subject.
☐ Keep cross-kind second-mount rejection at the shared mount-context boundary.
☐ Do not export a compatibility alias or alternate spelling.

### Phase 1 exit gate

☐ `ds.mountNativeScreen()` reaches the existing native attachment path.
☐ `ds.mount()` cannot enter native attachment through missing or nil input.
☐ Native-screen ownership, input, rendering, staleness, and cleanup code is
  otherwise unchanged.
☐ Every changed Lua declaration has LuaDoc.

## Phase 2: Public declarations and repository call sites

Goal: make the explicit API the only positive native-screen mounting form in
the repository.

☐ Add `DS.mountNativeScreen()` to `src/ds.d.lua` with a non-owning/current
  native-screen contract and borrowed root-subject return type.
☐ Remove the no-argument overload from the `DS.mount` declaration.
☐ Make the `DS.mount` parameter non-optional and document its owned component
  behavior.
☐ Replace positive native-screen calls in unit tests with
  `ds.mountNativeScreen()`.
☐ Replace the live acceptance call with `ds.mountNativeScreen()`.
☐ Retain intentional `ds.mount()` and `ds.mount(nil)` calls only in explicit
  rejection tests.
☐ Replace internal `mount_native` calls with `mount_native_screen`.
☐ Update no-current-mount diagnostics so they recognize either valid mount
  entry point where guidance is appropriate.
☐ Search source and tests for stale aliases or positive no-argument calls.

### Phase 2 exit gate

☐ LuaLS exposes separate component and native-screen mount commands.
☐ No executable positive path uses the removed overload.
☐ Rejection fixtures are the only remaining executable `ds.mount()` calls
  without a component.
☐ No duplicate native attachment implementation was introduced.

## Phase 3: Deterministic API coverage

Goal: prove the new boundary and preserve all existing native-screen behavior.

☐ Test that `ds.mountNativeScreen()` returns the exact borrowed native root
  subject.
☐ Test that it constructs, shows, resizes, replaces, and dismisses no screen.
☐ Test rejection of arguments to `ds.mountNativeScreen()`.
☐ Test actionable rejection of `ds.mount()` and `ds.mount(nil)`.
☐ Test component-to-native, native-to-component, and native-to-native
  second-mount rejection.
☐ Test explicit unmount followed by successful mounting through the other
  entry point.
☐ Preserve tests for native/overlay source selection, subject lookup,
  inspection, input, arbitrary pointer placement, redraw waiting, staleness,
  and LIFO cleanup.
☐ Preserve failure-path tests for attachment, observer installation, input,
  render, timeout, abort, runner recovery, and cleanup conflicts.
☐ Assert that the removed no-argument behavior is not exposed under another
  alias.
☐ Run the focused public mount-command, mount-context, and native-attachment
  unit specifications.

### Phase 3 exit gate

☐ Focused unit tests pass.
☐ Tests cover the new public success path and every removed-overload rejection
  path.
☐ Tests prove behavior and ownership invariants rather than only method
  presence.
☐ No packaging or editor-configuration test was added.

