## Phase 5: Full and live acceptance

Goal: verify deterministic behavior, real DFHack wiring, cleanup, and final
repository consistency.

☐ Run the focused public mount-command, mount-context, and native-attachment
  unit specifications.
☐ Run `.\tools\Run-UnitTests.ps1`.
☐ Run `.\tools\Check-Lua.ps1`.
☐ Run `git diff --check`.
☐ Run
  `.\tools\Run-AutomationTests.ps1 --test-glob tests/automation/native_screen_mount_live_spec.lua`
  for focused native-screen acceptance.
☐ Confirm the live test used `ds.mountNativeScreen()` and observed the exact
  current native viewscreen and widget root.
☐ Confirm live cleanup preserved the original screen, focus, stack, pointer
  state, overlay registration, and render instrumentation.
☐ Confirm no DwarfSpec-owned or test-owned screen remains after the live run.
☐ If live DFHack is unavailable, record the exact environmental blocker and
  leave live acceptance incomplete; deterministic tests are not a substitute.
☐ Search source, declarations, tests, and documentation for stale positive
  no-argument mount usage and old `mount_native` identifiers.
☐ Review the diff for accidental attachment, adapter, observer, transport,
  scheduler, persistence, CLI, version, or in-game UI changes.
☐ Review `git status --short` and account for every changed file.
☐ Complete the evidence ledger and final acceptance only after every required
  check passes.

### Phase 5 exit gate

☐ Focused and full unit tests pass.
☐ Lua syntax and formatting checks pass.
☐ Focused live native-screen acceptance passes with confirmed cleanup.
☐ Diff hygiene, stale-reference searches, and worktree accounting pass.
☐ Every earlier phase and exit gate is complete.

