## Final acceptance

☐ `ds.mountNativeScreen()` is the only public native-screen mount entry point.
☐ `ds.mount(component, options)` cannot attach to a native screen.
☐ No compatibility alias or deprecated no-argument behavior remains.
☐ Both mount entry points share one current mount and `ds.unmount()` lifecycle.
☐ Native-screen subjects and commands retain their existing behavior.
☐ Native screens, focus, stack, overlays, input state, and instrumentation
  retain their existing ownership and cleanup guarantees.
☐ Public declarations, implementation, tests, and documentation agree.
☐ Deterministic and live verification pass with fresh evidence.
☐ All checklist and evidence-ledger items are complete.
